-- title:
--   Scalar normalisation making a modular function a unit of the localised reduction
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a natural number assumed prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$, and let $\mathrm{red}\colon A \to k$ be a ring homomorphism. Write $N = 1\cdot q$ and let $f$ be a nonzero element of `modularFunctionFieldBar` $N$, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}(\!(\mathfrak q)\!)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the coefficientwise image of the field $\mathbb Q$-generated by the divisor expansions of level $N$. Let $\mathcal O =$ `modularLocalized` $N$ $A$ $\mathrm{red}$ be the subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}(\!(\mathfrak q)\!)$ consisting of those Laurent series $g$ for which $g\,s = r$ for some $r,s$ in the subring generated by the constant series with coefficients in $A$ together with the two series `jqModC` and `jqNModC` of level $N$, with $s$ outside the (prime) kernel of coefficientwise reduction; and let $\pi =$ `modularRedLocHom` $N$ $A$ $\mathrm{red}\colon \mathcal O \to k(\!(\mathfrak q)\!)$ be the induced reduction homomorphism. The assertion is that there exists $c \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $c \neq 0$ such that the Laurent series underlying $c \cdot f$ lies in $\mathcal O$ and its image under $\pi$ is nonzero.
--
--   This is the Gauss normalisation step: intersected with the modular function field, $\mathcal O$ is the valuation ring of the Gauss valuation attached to the component of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(q)$ through the cusp $\infty$, so after scaling by a suitable leading constant every nonzero modular function becomes a unit there. It is invoked in the construction of two-branch normalisations at the nodes of the special fibre, via [`ModularCurve.coe_mem_modularLocalized_or_coe_inv_mem_modularLocalized`](thm.html#ModularCurve.coe_mem_modularLocalized_or_coe_inv_mem_modularLocalized) and the regular prolongation statement [`ModularCurve.exists_regularProlongation_modularFunctionFieldBar_self`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_regularProlongation_modularFunctionFieldBar_self).
